    "linkedin:b7d3743b07d0390bb9a0614d": {
      "job": {
        "title": "React Developer",
        "company": "Wiraa",
        "location": "",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4476384896",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": true,
        "description": "**About The Company**\n Bright Vision Technologies is a leading technology consulting and software development firm specializing in delivering innovative cloud, artificial intelligence, data management, and enterprise solutions across the United States. With a strong commitment to excellence and a customer\\-centric approach, Bright Vision Technologies has established itself as a trusted partner for organizations seeking scalable and cutting\\-edge digital solutions. The company prides itself on fostering a collaborative work environment that encourages continuous learning, innovation, and professional growth. Their portfolio includes a diverse range of projects spanning financial services, healthcare, insurance, and enterprise workflow automation, leveraging the latest technologies to meet complex business needs.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Role**\n We are seeking an experienced React Developer to join our dynamic team in a fully remote capacity within the U.S. This full\\-time, direct W2 position offers an excellent opportunity to work on high\\-impact enterprise web applications that serve thousands of users. As a React Developer at Bright Vision Technologies, you will be responsible for designing, developing, and maintaining modern, scalable, and responsive Single Page Applications (SPAs). Your work will involve integrating front\\-end components with enterprise APIs, cloud\\-native services, and microservices architectures to deliver seamless user experiences across various devices and browsers. Collaboration with cross\\-functional teams including product managers, UX/UI designers, backend engineers, and DevOps is essential to ensure the delivery of high\\-quality solutions. This role provides significant career growth potential within a respected organization dedicated to technological innovation and excellence.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Qualifications**\n* Minimum of 5\\+ years of professional front\\-end development experience\n* At least 4\\+ years of hands\\-on experience building enterprise applications with React\n* Proficiency in React 18\\+ and modern JavaScript (ES6\\+)\n* Strong TypeScript skills\n* Deep understanding of React Hooks, Functional Components, Context API, Suspense, Error Boundaries, and component lifecycle methods\n* Experience with state management libraries such as Redux Toolkit, Redux, Zustand, React Query, or Context API\n* Solid knowledge of HTML5, CSS3, SCSS, Tailwind CSS, Styled Components, or CSS Modules\n* Experience integrating RESTful APIs and GraphQL services\n* Familiarity with authentication protocols including OAuth2, OpenID Connect, Azure Active Directory, Okta, or Auth0\n* Understanding of responsive web design, accessibility standards (WCAG), semantic HTML, and cross\\-browser compatibility\n* Experience working with modern build tools such as Vite, Webpack, Babel, npm, and Yarn\n* Proficiency with version control systems like Git and collaboration platforms such as GitHub, Azure DevOps, GitLab, or Bitbucket\n* Experience with CI/CD pipelines using platforms like GitHub Actions, Azure DevOps, Jenkins, or GitLab CI\n* Strong debugging skills with browser developer tools, Lighthouse, and performance profiling tools\n* Experience consuming backend services built with .NET Core, Java Spring Boot, Node.js, or Python\n* Experience working within Agile Scrum development environments\n\n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Design, develop, and maintain enterprise\\-grade Single Page Applications (SPAs) using React and TypeScript\n* Create reusable, scalable, and maintainable UI components following enterprise design standards\n* Develop responsive web applications optimized for desktop, tablet, and mobile devices\n* Integrate applications with RESTful APIs, GraphQL services, and cloud\\-native backend platforms\n* Collaborate with UX/UI designers to translate designs from Figma or Adobe XD into accessible, pixel\\-perfect interfaces\n* Implement efficient client\\-side state management strategies using Redux Toolkit, React Query, or Context API\n* Optimize application performance through techniques such as lazy loading, code splitting, memoization, and virtualization\n* Develop secure authentication and authorization workflows using OAuth2, OpenID Connect, Azure AD, Okta, or Auth0\n* Implement real\\-time features utilizing WebSockets, SignalR, or Server\\-Sent Events (SSE)\n* Create reusable custom hooks, utility libraries, and shared component packages to promote code consistency\n* Conduct unit, integration, and end\\-to\\-end testing to ensure application reliability and maintainability\n* Participate in architecture and code reviews, sprint planning, and technical discussions within Agile teams\n* Troubleshoot and resolve production issues, browser compatibility challenges, and front\\-end performance bottlenecks\n* Collaborate with DevOps teams to automate deployment processes via CI/CD pipelines\n\n\n**Benefits**\n* Competitive salary range of $120,000–$180,000 annually\n* 100% remote work opportunity within the U.S.\n* Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance plans\n* Paid time off and holidays\n* Professional development opportunities and continuous learning support\n* Flexible work hours to promote work\\-life balance\n* Collaborative and innovative work environment\n* Opportunities for career advancement within a growing organization\n\n\n Equal Opportunity\n   \n\n  \n\n We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal, state, or local law.",
