    "linkedin:e94f2cb1f8453d0677d62c72": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Web Developer",
        "company": "Netrolynx AI",
        "location": "",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4476356428",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": false,
        "description": "**About The Company**\n Sierra is a pioneering platform specializing in customer\\-facing AI agents, collaborating with some of the world's most prominent brands including The GAP, Rocket Mortgage, SoFi, Sutter Health, and SoftBank. Our mission is to revolutionize customer service and business growth through innovative AI solutions. Headquartered in San Francisco, Sierra maintains a strong physical presence with expanding offices across North America, Europe, and Asia. Our company culture is rooted in core values that include Trust, Customer Obsession, Craftsmanship, Intensity, and a commitment to fostering a balanced Family environment. These principles guide our daily operations and long\\-term vision, ensuring we deliver exceptional products and services while nurturing a supportive workplace environment.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Role**\n We are seeking a talented and dedicated Frontend Developer to join Sierra’s dynamic team. This role offers an exciting opportunity to influence both our core product interface and our customer\\-facing web presence. The ideal candidate will be responsible for creating seamless, engaging, and accessible user experiences across multiple platforms. You will collaborate closely with cross\\-functional teams including marketing, design, and product management to develop and optimize features that drive growth and enhance user satisfaction. Your work will directly impact how our clients and end\\-users interact with Sierra’s innovative AI solutions, ensuring that our digital touchpoints are both visually appealing and highly functional.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Qualifications**\n The ideal candidate will possess a strong foundation in frontend development with a focus on performance, accessibility, and user experience. Experience working with marketing and growth\\-oriented web projects is essential, along with proficiency in modern JavaScript, TypeScript, and frameworks such as React or similar. Familiarity with headless CMS platforms like Sanity, structured content models, and localization processes is highly desirable. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to optimizing web performance and accessibility, with a track record of implementing best practices. Excellent collaboration skills are necessary to effectively work with non\\-engineering teams, translating their goals into technical solutions. A genuine interest in continuous learning and improvement is also valued.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Own frontend development across product and marketing surfaces, ensuring a cohesive and polished user experience. This includes building features within the web application and collaborating on website updates to maintain consistent branding and high\\-quality design standards.\n* Develop and enhance content infrastructure by designing and implementing CMS schemas, editing workflows, and preview/staging environments. Empower content and marketing teams with self\\-serve tools that reduce dependency on engineering for routine updates.\n* Partner with marketing, sales, and operations teams to implement analytics, enable experimentation, and translate business objectives into measurable, shipped features. Use data\\-driven insights to continually optimize user engagement and conversion rates.\n* Support localization and internationalization efforts by developing multilingual content workflows, translation management systems, and infrastructure that deliver high\\-quality experiences for global audiences.\n* Prioritize performance as a core feature by managing Core Web Vitals, optimizing media assets, diagnosing subtle performance issues, and ensuring fast load times and smooth interactions.\n* Champion accessibility standards by implementing semantic markup, keyboard navigation, screen\\-reader support, and WCAG\\-compliant component design, making our digital platforms usable for all visitors.\n\n\n**Benefits**\n Sierra offers a comprehensive benefits package designed to reflect our values and support our employees' well\\-being. Full\\-time employees enjoy flexible, unlimited paid time off, comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for themselves and their families, and life insurance and disability benefits. Our retirement plans vary by region, and we provide generous parental leave and fertility benefits through Carrot. Employees also benefit from daily meals, snacks, and coffee to stay energized, a discretionary stipend to support personal needs, and unique perks such as free alphorn lessons. These benefits are subject to regional variations and may evolve over time, aligning with Sierra’s commitment to fostering a supportive and inclusive work environment.\n   \n\n  \n\n Equal Opportunity\n   \n\n  \n\n Sierra is committed to creating an inclusive workplace where diversity is celebrated and every individual is valued. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate based on race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other protected class. We encourage applicants from all backgrounds to apply and are dedicated to providing a supportive environment that enables all employees to thrive and succeed.",
